{
  "rules": [
    "Persistent low bias: across most horizons the model underpredicts the true path by ~+1 to +3 EUR, especially during rising regimes. Apply an upward level shift when the last 10–15 days show a positive trend (e.g., price above 10–20d MA).",
    "Trend underreaction / lag: when the market breaks upward (fast rally), the model follows but too slowly; errors grow with horizon (mid-to-late forecast window). Add a trend term that increases with forecast step (e.g., +0.05 to +0.12 EUR per day during uptrends).",
    "Over-mean-reversion after spikes: the model often fades strength too aggressively (forecasts dip back toward mid-60s while realized stays high-60s). Reduce mean-reversion strength when realized volatility is elevated and recent returns are positive.",
    "Horizon-specific bias: early horizon (days 1–7) errors are smaller; days ~8–25 show the largest underprediction. Use a piecewise correction: small uplift near-term, larger uplift mid-horizon, then taper late-horizon.",
    "Downside overshoot in some late horizons: in a few cases the model projects a drop to low-60s while realized remains mid/high-60s. Impose a floor tied to recent support (e.g., not below min(last 10 days) + 0.5–1.0 EUR) during uptrends."
  ]
}
